<title>USA: Stolt-Nielsen to buy back 500,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Stolt-Nielsen to buy back 500,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stolt-Nielsen SA said Monday it would buy back up to 500,000 shares of its common stock, its Class B shares, and/or related American Depository shares.</p>
<p>The shares are to be repurchased from time to time in the open market when the company considers the share price attractive.</p>
<p>The shares to be repurchased will offset shares issued or to be issued in connection with employee stock-option plans, it said.  </p>
<p>Stolt-Nielsen, which is based in London, provides transportation services for bulk liquid chemicals, edible oils, acids and other specialty liquids.</p>
</text>
